## COMMUNICATION
MoP nanoparticles supported on Indoped porous carbon had outstanding performance for ${\mathsf{C O}}_{2}$ reduction to formate. The Faradaic efficiency and current density could reach $96.5\%$ and $43.8~\mathsf{m A}\cdot\mathsf{c m}^{-2}$ , respectively, when using ionic liquid as the supporting electrolyte. The current density is higher than those reported up to date with very high Faradaic efficiency. MoP and In-doped carbon support had exellent synergistic effect for promoting this reaction.
